@@text Script-only except the Storage Delight name (repackedStorage jar rebuilt 2026-10-29, not installed: a game was running). Recipe checks need a full restart (removed_items.js, order.js are startup scripts).
@@text
@@table
## SQ-CM-30 | no fruit beignet
@group A
@commands boot with current kubejs; recipe id dump
@pass no recipe outputs or takes `rusticdelight:fruit_beignet`; no errors from `rusticdelight/recipes.js` or `removed_items.js`
@fails `creativedelight/members #22`
@from batches/r1031/a1_data.qb passed
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> cdevtest makes rusticdelight:fruit_beignet
> cdevtest uses rusticdelight:fruit_beignet
expect verb=makes item=rusticdelight:fruit_beignet n=0
# judge-5, 2026-11-18: the item is gone from the registry now: uses answers 'no such item' with done=0
expect verb=uses (item=rusticdelight:fruit_beignet alone=0 shared=0|error="no such item rusticdelight:fruit_beignet")
kjsreject (rusticdelight/recipes\.js|removed_items\.js).*(Error|error)
reject verb=makes .*done=0

## SQ-CM-31 | seagrass salad, no tentacles anywhere
@group A
@commands same probe
@pass `oceansdelight:seagrass_salad` recipe is `creativedelight:shapeless/seagrass_salad` with 2 `minecraft:seagrass` + bowl; no tentacle item (`miners_delight:tentacles`, `baked_tentacles`, `tentacles_on_a_stick`, `oceansdelight:tentacles`, `cut_tentacles`, `tentacle_on_a_stick`, `baked_tentacle_on_a_stick`, `oceanic_delight:squid_tentacles`, `glow_squid_tentacles`, `grilled_squid_tentacles`) is an output or input of any recipe (`/recipescan`)
@fails `creativedelight/members #24`, `dishes/ocean #4`
@from batches/r1031/a1_data.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> cdevtest rdetail seagrass_salad
> cdevtest uses miners_delight:tentacles
> cdevtest uses miners_delight:baked_tentacles
> cdevtest uses oceansdelight:tentacles
> cdevtest uses oceansdelight:cut_tentacles
> cdevtest uses oceanic_delight:squid_tentacles
> cdevtest uses oceanic_delight:glow_squid_tentacles
> cdevtest makes tentacle
expect creativedelight:shapeless/seagrass_salad
# judge-5, 2026-11-18: cdevtest uses prints alone=N shared=N now
count verb=uses item=\S+ alone=0 shared=0 == 6
expect verb=makes item=tentacle n=0
look seagrass salad takes 2 minecraft:seagrass + bowl; the 4 tentacle-on-a-stick and grilled ids are covered by "makes tentacle"
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0

## SQ-CM-32 | tentacle dishes take calamari
@group A
@commands same probe
@pass `oceansdelight:cooking/squid_rings`, `oceanic_delight:sea_pickle_roll`, `shrimp_rice`, `squid_salad`, `takoyaki` take `#forge:raw_fishes/calamari`; `glow_squid_stew` takes `#forge:raw_fishes/calamari` (glowing and every slice included); `seafood_skewer`, `squid_and_pickles` take `#forge:cooked_fishes/calamari` (the tag replace in the four `#forge:squid_tentacles` recipes is the part most likely to miss)
@fails replaceInput on a tag
@from batches/r1031/a1_data.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> cdevtest rdetail squid_rings
> cdevtest rdetail sea_pickle_roll
> cdevtest rdetail shrimp_rice
> cdevtest rdetail squid_salad
> cdevtest rdetail takoyaki
> cdevtest rdetail glow_squid_stew
> cdevtest rdetail seafood_skewer
> cdevtest rdetail squid_and_pickles
look each takes #forge:raw_fishes/calamari (seafood_skewer, squid_and_pickles: #forge:cooked_fishes/calamari); rdetail lists the tag's first items, so a calamari item there = PASS, a tentacle = FAIL
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0

## SQ-CM-33 | (server half) no tag error naming the Storage Delight JEI tag; the tag holds the 140 blocks
@group A
@commands boot; JEI item list (client)
@pass the 140 Storage Delight blocks sit together in wood order (oak, spruce, birch, jungle, acacia, dark oak, mangrove, crimson, warped, bamboo); no tag error naming `creativecommon:jei/storage_delight`
@fails `creativedelight/members #23`
@from batches/r1113/c1_a1.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
# id fix: the tag is creativecompat:jei/storage_delight since the 2026-11-09 namespace move (row says creativecommon:)
bootreject (?i)(error|fail|unknown|invalid|missing).*(creativecompat|creativecommon|creativeengineering):jei/storage_delight
> cdevtest tag item creativecompat:jei/storage_delight
waitlog verb=tag kind=item tag=creativecompat:jei/storage_delight n= 30
expect verb=tag kind=item tag=creativecompat:jei/storage_delight n=140 
look client half (JEI item list in wood order) stays open: CQ row / client run
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0

## SQ-CM-34
@group A
@commands after the repackedStorage install; mod list
@pass Storage Delight shows as "Storage Delight (Creative Delight)"
@fails jar not installed
@reviewed 2026-11-16
shell grep -hoE "Storage Delight[^\"]*" logs/latest.log | sort -u | head -3; unzip -p mods/repackedStorage*.jar META-INF/mods.toml 2>/dev/null | grep -E "displayName"
look shell: displayName is "Storage Delight (Creative Delight)"; the mod list name itself is a client screen
## SQ-CM-35 | calamari tags and dishes (with SQ-CM-32)
@group A
@commands boot with the 2026-10-31 12:32 CD jar; recipe probe + kubejs/startup.log and latest.log
@pass `#forge:squid_tentacles` and `#forge:foods/tentacles` hold the raw calamari items; `miners_delight:cooking/takoyaki` takes calamari in both tentacle slots; `squid_rings`, `glow_squid_stew`, `seafood_skewer`, `squid_and_pickles` exist (rerun SQ-CM-32 alongside); no `[NCH]` error naming `squid_tentacles` or `truffle_pie`
@fails `dishes/ocean #4`
@from batches/r1101/p1_server.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> cdevtest tag item forge:squid_tentacles
> cdevtest tag item forge:foods/tentacles
> cdevtest rdetail takoyaki
> cdevtest rdetail squid_rings
> cdevtest rdetail glow_squid_stew
> cdevtest rdetail seafood_skewer
> cdevtest rdetail squid_and_pickles
> cdevtest rdetail sea_pickle_roll
> cdevtest rdetail shrimp_rice
> cdevtest rdetail squid_salad
bootreject \[NCH\].*(squid_tentacles|truffle_pie)
expect squid_rings
expect glow_squid_stew
expect seafood_skewer
expect squid_and_pickles
look both tags hold raw calamari; takoyaki (miners_delight) takes calamari in both slots; no empty slots
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0

## SQ-CM-36
@group A
@commands same boot; recipe probe, `/fgdtest all`, then a client
@pass `create_central_kitchen:truffle_pie` is an item (Truffle Pie, chocolate pie sprite) that places CCK's truffle pie block; `creativedelight:baking/truffle_pie` exists and takes `fungidelight:truffle`; the placed pie gives truffle pie slices; `/fgdtest` oven truffle pie PASS; no `[NCH] ceBaking ... truffle_pie` error and no `truffle_pie` in the item_dict missing-id list
@fails `ports/fungiport #3`
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> cdevtest item create_central_kitchen:truffle_pie
> cdevtest rdetail creativedelight:baking/truffle_pie
> fgdtest all
sleep 10
> forceload add 0 0 15 15
> setblock 4 -60 4 create_central_kitchen:truffle_pie
> cdevtest use 4 -60 4 held=farmersdelight:iron_knife
> cdevtest items 4 -60 4 3
expect verb=item item=create_central_kitchen:truffle_pie class=\S+ .*block=create_central_kitchen:truffle_pie
expect verb=rdetail id=creativedelight:baking/truffle_pie .*ingredients=\S*fungidelight:truffle
expect verb=items items=\S*truffle_pie_slice:1\b
bootreject \[NCH\] ceBaking .*truffle_pie
bootreject \[item_dict\] Missing.*truffle_pie
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0
look the /fgdtest oven truffle pie line is PASS; Truffle Pie name and the chocolate pie sprite are client (CQ)
